WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.000 --> 00:00:06.140
Hey youtubers it's Charlie and since Korra
is on break this weekend I wanted to do a

00:00:06.140 --> 00:00:08.510
bonus video for Book 4.

00:00:08.510 --> 00:00:12.010
Because of all the craziness going on with
Book 3 right now I thought it would be helpful

00:00:12.010 --> 00:00:15.330
to put it all into context and talk about
some things we can all be really happy about.

00:00:15.330 --> 00:00:19.750
And Just for fun I'm going to rank my top
10 last airbender characters.

00:00:19.750 --> 00:00:22.760
Congrats to last weeks giveaway winners.

00:00:22.760 --> 00:00:29.189
Effective Kill, Khaler Jex and Novelist Vampire
Girl you guys each win an amazon gift card.

00:00:29.189 --> 00:00:31.789
I'll be messaging you on your channels for
details.

00:00:31.789 --> 00:00:34.130
So check your inboxes today.

00:00:34.130 --> 00:00:36.989
Even though there's no new episode I'm continuing
the giveaway this week.

00:00:36.989 --> 00:00:41.040
All you have to do to participate is be a
subscriber and leave a comment on this video.

00:00:41.040 --> 00:00:46.180
There's only one winner per episode, that's
why there were three people from last week.

00:00:46.180 --> 00:00:49.309
Which brings up a good point, what's going
on with Book 3 right now.

00:00:49.309 --> 00:00:53.560
Nick just casually dropped that they'd be
doubling up on Korra episodes indefinitely.

00:00:53.560 --> 00:00:55.739
They didn't say "for the rest of the season".

00:00:55.739 --> 00:01:00.820
But the next several episodes, through episode
7 at least, they'll be doing two episodes

00:01:00.820 --> 00:01:02.540
back to back each week.

00:01:02.540 --> 00:01:05.960
So next week when it comes back on Friday
July 11th, they'll air episodes 4 and 5 together,

00:01:05.960 --> 00:01:08.479
then the week after that 6 and 7.

00:01:08.479 --> 00:01:13.450
By the time we get to 6 and 7 they'll probably
announce if they're going to keep doing two

00:01:13.450 --> 00:01:15.940
per week, I really hope they don't.

00:01:15.940 --> 00:01:18.250
It's awesome to get an hour of Korra every
week.

00:01:18.250 --> 00:01:22.680
But think about it this way, the faster they
burn through Korra episodes, the longer the

00:01:22.680 --> 00:01:24.590
wait will be till Book 4.

00:01:24.590 --> 00:01:27.950
And there's been no indication that they're
going to tell us when Book 4 is going to premiere.

00:01:27.950 --> 00:01:30.020
So Book 4 discussion time.

00:01:30.020 --> 00:01:31.210
Here is my thought.

00:01:31.210 --> 00:01:39.060
In light of the weirdness that has been going
on with the Book 3 leaks and lack of promotion.

00:01:39.060 --> 00:01:42.210
Nick is going to hold off airing Book 4 until
next year.

00:01:42.210 --> 00:01:46.630
And use that extra time to promote the series
the way they should have promoted Book 3.

00:01:46.630 --> 00:01:51.420
Master Sifu was on twitter talking about going
in for Korra Marketing meetings with the studio

00:01:51.420 --> 00:01:54.590
recently, so if they're bringing him in to
help figure out a better way to promote the

00:01:54.590 --> 00:01:57.909
series it means they are dedicating resources
to the problem.

00:01:57.909 --> 00:01:59.930
Which makes me a lot more excited.

00:01:59.930 --> 00:02:05.040
I feel like the fandom will always do a better
job of creating awareness, but Nick is the

00:02:05.040 --> 00:02:09.179
one with the resources to actually put ads
in big places so that the general public knows

00:02:09.179 --> 00:02:11.610
when and where to find new Korra episodes.

00:02:11.610 --> 00:02:15.120
One of the really cool things that networks
have started to do in the last couple of years

00:02:15.120 --> 00:02:20.060
is rely on stars with big social accounts
like on Twitter and Facebook to drive engagement

00:02:20.060 --> 00:02:21.250
with the fandom and call everyone to action.

00:02:21.250 --> 00:02:23.280
The best example of this is Vin Diesel.

00:02:23.280 --> 00:02:31.560
He used his own money to make that last Riddick
movie and he said the one big reason enough

00:02:31.560 --> 00:02:37.120
people came out to see the movie was because
he was able to reach his huge facebook audience.

00:02:37.120 --> 00:02:38.560
His page has like 80 Million followers.

00:02:38.560 --> 00:02:45.610
Crazy right, so if you ever wanted to fund
like a new season of Korra or a Korra movie,

00:02:45.610 --> 00:02:50.530
just build a giant audience somewhere on social
and crowd fund it.

00:02:50.530 --> 00:02:55.660
Here's a good question for all you guys, if
I ever got to the point where I had some crazy

00:02:55.660 --> 00:02:59.560
number of subscribers here on my channel like
10 Million.

00:02:59.560 --> 00:03:02.520
And I had the chance to crowd fund something.

00:03:02.520 --> 00:03:04.830
What would you want to see me bring back?

00:03:04.830 --> 00:03:09.670
I'm so far away from being able to do something
like that, but it's a really fun fantasy to

00:03:09.670 --> 00:03:10.670
have.

00:03:10.670 --> 00:03:14.510
I'd like to think that someday if I work hard
enough I could take something I really love

00:03:14.510 --> 00:03:16.380
and bring it back from the dead.

00:03:16.380 --> 00:03:30.610
So the big takeaway from all this book 3 weirdness
is that we should be optimistic that magical

00:03:30.610 --> 00:03:33.260
things will happen when Book 4 gets closer.

00:03:33.260 --> 00:03:37.561
So because it's the weekend and we all need
to have some fun let's rank our favorite Last

00:03:37.561 --> 00:03:38.561
Airbender characters.

00:03:38.561 --> 00:03:39.561
Because a lot of them have been appearing
on Korra.

00:03:39.561 --> 00:03:40.561
I'm going to start at

00:03:40.561 --> 00:03:42.590
Number 10 - Zhao

00:03:42.590 --> 00:03:45.810
He's currently still stuck in the fog of Lost
Souls as of the end of book 2.

00:03:45.810 --> 00:03:47.030
I think he's still stuck in there.

00:03:47.030 --> 00:03:49.959
I'm not expecting him to appear again but
I feel like Jason Isaacs brought so much to

00:03:49.959 --> 00:03:51.150
this character.

00:03:51.150 --> 00:03:52.840
He's so good at playing villains.

00:03:52.840 --> 00:03:56.879
And Zhao's voice was so distinct that I feel
like everyone went a little nuts when he showed

00:03:56.879 --> 00:03:57.910
up on Korra.

00:03:57.910 --> 00:04:01.640
Jason Isaacs even returned during book 1 to
voice new lines for the character in Book

00:04:01.640 --> 00:04:04.269
1 episode 13.

00:04:04.269 --> 00:04:08.599
I don't know if they just used a dub of his
voice for the scenes in Book 2 in the Fog

00:04:08.599 --> 00:04:14.400
of Lost souls, but it's pretty cool that he
came back at all.

00:04:14.400 --> 00:04:16.030
My favorite Zhao scene was either his death
during Last Airbender or finding out he was

00:04:16.030 --> 00:04:19.400
stuck in the Fog of Lost souls.

00:04:19.400 --> 00:04:22.470
Number 9 - Suki of the Kyoshi Warriors

00:04:22.470 --> 00:04:26.860
As of right now, she's the only original Team
Avatar person who hasn't been mentioned or

00:04:26.860 --> 00:04:28.250
seen on Korra.

00:04:28.250 --> 00:04:30.440
She was always a character I thought deserved
more screen time.

00:04:30.440 --> 00:04:34.130
She is in the Search comic, but otherwise
we're still waiting to find out what her final

00:04:34.130 --> 00:04:36.640
fate was and if she ever ended up with Sokka.

00:04:36.640 --> 00:04:42.150
Fun Fact, she's also the only origina team
avatar members to not get a solo field trip

00:04:42.150 --> 00:04:43.150
with Zuko.

00:04:43.150 --> 00:04:47.400
Each of the other characters got a Zuko side
story when it was just them and Zuko.

00:04:47.400 --> 00:04:49.730
But she was never a huge fan of his.

00:04:49.730 --> 00:04:55.360
Originally the plan for her character was
that she would only appear in that first Kyoshi

00:04:55.360 --> 00:04:58.139
Warrior episode, it was Book 1 episode 4.

00:04:58.139 --> 00:05:02.031
But people like her so much Mike and Bryan
made her an official member of team Avatar

00:05:02.031 --> 00:05:03.031
in books 2 and 3.

00:05:03.031 --> 00:05:06.191
I think my favorite Suki moment was during
the ember island players episode where she

00:05:06.191 --> 00:05:10.780
tried to sneak backstage to make the actor
playing her act better.

00:05:10.780 --> 00:05:13.169
Number 8 - Sokka

00:05:13.169 --> 00:05:18.440
It actually took me a little while to get
used to how over the top he was all the time.

00:05:18.440 --> 00:05:20.820
He was always the character that reacted to
things.

00:05:20.820 --> 00:05:24.750
Like Aang was in this constant state of child-like
wonder about things, Katara was the voice

00:05:24.750 --> 00:05:27.360
of reason and Sokka was always the one who
would have the WTF style reactions.

00:05:27.360 --> 00:05:28.360
I really loved him more when they made it
to the Northern Water Tribe and after the

00:05:28.360 --> 00:05:29.360
Suki character was introduced.

00:05:29.360 --> 00:05:30.360
If feel like that's when he matured a little
and started to get more hero moments.

00:05:30.360 --> 00:05:34.889
My favorite Sokka moment was in Book 3 where
he and Katara had to attend Aang's Fire Nation

00:05:34.889 --> 00:05:37.520
parent teacher conference as Mr Wang Fire.

00:05:37.520 --> 00:05:38.520
But here's an interesting thought.

00:05:38.520 --> 00:05:42.980
If Sokka were still alive today, do you think
he would have been one of the people to gain

00:05:42.980 --> 00:05:43.980
airbending?

00:05:43.980 --> 00:05:45.800
He was from the water tribe, so there's no
guarantee he would have.

00:05:45.800 --> 00:05:51.110
But if they let Bumi become an airbender I
supposed it's possible.

00:05:51.110 --> 00:05:53.400
Number 7 - Firelord Ozai

00:05:53.400 --> 00:05:54.720
Shoutout to Mark Hamill.

00:05:54.720 --> 00:05:58.620
His Ozai was dramatically different from the
other voices he's done, but just think about

00:05:58.620 --> 00:06:01.330
the idea of Firelord Joker.

00:06:01.330 --> 00:06:03.370
Ozai did go a little bananas at the end.

00:06:03.370 --> 00:06:09.889
I loved his arc up to the appearance of Sozin's
Comet when he declared himself the Phoenix

00:06:09.889 --> 00:06:13.270
King.

00:06:13.270 --> 00:06:17.479
In case you haven't read a lot of the backstory,
Ozai and his father Firelord Azulon wanted

00:06:17.479 --> 00:06:24.039
to bond the Avatar's lineage to theirs so
Ozai married Ursa, Avatar Roku's granddaughter.

00:06:24.039 --> 00:06:25.180
Zuko's mother.

00:06:25.180 --> 00:06:29.450
So technically you could say that Zoku is
linked to Korra on a spiritual level, even

00:06:29.450 --> 00:06:31.639
if she's been separated from her past lives.

00:06:31.639 --> 00:06:36.030
I also know a lot of you haven't read The
Search comic, that's the one that tells what

00:06:36.030 --> 00:06:37.650
happened to Zuko's mother.

00:06:37.650 --> 00:06:43.979
So read it if you want to know.

00:06:43.979 --> 00:06:46.560
He does find her at the end.

00:06:46.560 --> 00:06:49.350
Number 6 - Azula

00:06:49.350 --> 00:06:51.940
She genuinely had some non-evil person moments.

00:06:51.940 --> 00:06:54.830
Like when they went to Ember Island and she
tried to pick up that boy.

00:06:54.830 --> 00:06:56.050
Best Azula pickup line.

00:06:56.050 --> 00:06:57.740
"That's a sharp outfit there.

00:06:57.740 --> 00:07:01.590
Careful, you could puncture the hull of an
empire class fire nation ship.

00:07:01.590 --> 00:07:03.889
Leaving thousands to drown at sea."

00:07:03.889 --> 00:07:05.960
So hard to figure out why she's still single?

00:07:05.960 --> 00:07:10.900
I know everyone is curious if sparky sparky
boom girl on Korra is related to her just

00:07:10.900 --> 00:07:12.700
because of the visual similarity.

00:07:12.700 --> 00:07:19.419
I don't think that's the case, but I do think
we'll find out what happened to Azula by book

00:07:19.419 --> 00:07:20.419
4.

00:07:20.419 --> 00:07:23.310
Number 5 - Katara

00:07:23.310 --> 00:07:26.500
She was everyone's mom even before she became
an actual mom.

00:07:26.500 --> 00:07:31.210
I always liked when Mike and Bryan let her
have fun and she didn't have to be the responsible

00:07:31.210 --> 00:07:32.210
one.

00:07:32.210 --> 00:07:33.850
That was kind of her role on Team Avatar.

00:07:33.850 --> 00:07:39.620
Make sure ADHD Aang focused on the task at
hand and make sure Sokka didn't get himself

00:07:39.620 --> 00:07:40.620
killed.

00:07:40.620 --> 00:07:43.800
And she doubled as the healer.

00:07:43.800 --> 00:07:48.349
We saw her use her healing ability during
Korra last season, and even though we haven't

00:07:48.349 --> 00:07:51.449
seen her yet in Book 3, I think she'll be
back soon.

00:07:51.449 --> 00:07:56.070
My favorite Katara moment was from The Fortuneteller
episode where she sees Aang super bend the

00:07:56.070 --> 00:08:04.180
volcano lava flow and realizes he might be
the powerful bender she's destined to marry.

00:08:04.180 --> 00:08:05.800
Number 4 - Iroh

00:08:05.800 --> 00:08:08.970
I was so happy when he showed up in the spirit
world.

00:08:08.970 --> 00:08:12.180
If there was any character who deserved to
get that kind of an ending it was him.

00:08:12.180 --> 00:08:16.460
He kind of reminds me of what Darth Vader
would have been had he not died.

00:08:16.460 --> 00:08:20.290
Like maybe if Luke had died like Iroh's son,
maybe he would have killed the Emperor and

00:08:20.290 --> 00:08:21.639
started helping the rebellion.

00:08:21.639 --> 00:08:26.039
I love Mark Hamill but I think I would have
rather seen that version of Star Wars.

00:08:26.039 --> 00:08:31.150
I'm not expecting to see Iroh again on Legend
of Korra, I think Zuko is filling the role

00:08:31.150 --> 00:08:33.650
he would normally occupy now.

00:08:33.650 --> 00:08:35.860
Especially since he's connected to the White
Lotus.

00:08:35.860 --> 00:08:40.740
My favorite Iroh moment was when he was stuck
in prison and started to train secretly when

00:08:40.740 --> 00:08:41.820
the guards weren't watching him.

00:08:41.820 --> 00:08:47.020
It's like you were just waiting for him to
tear shit up.

00:08:47.020 --> 00:08:48.839
Number 3 - Aang

00:08:48.839 --> 00:08:52.290
Yes he was the protagonist of the series,
but I feel like saying the main character

00:08:52.290 --> 00:08:54.560
was the most interesting is a cop out.

00:08:54.560 --> 00:08:57.990
He was one of my favorites and one of the
most interesting ones.

00:08:57.990 --> 00:09:02.190
He's been a huge part of Legend of Korra,
even when he's not on screen in spirit form.

00:09:02.190 --> 00:09:06.170
Only characters that had a deep connection
to the spirit world end up there, so I'm hoping

00:09:06.170 --> 00:09:08.040
we get to see him again that way.

00:09:08.040 --> 00:09:12.390
But it's implied that Korra will never reconnect
with her past lives, so I think if we see

00:09:12.390 --> 00:09:15.710
him any time soon on Korra it will be in a
flashback.

00:09:15.710 --> 00:09:21.650
And most of the flashbacks this season are
Beifong flashbacks.

00:09:21.650 --> 00:09:25.430
My favorite Aang moment was when the Lion
Turtle taught him to Energy Bend.

00:09:25.430 --> 00:09:28.930
He would have learned it from Guru Pathik
but left early to help his friends.

00:09:28.930 --> 00:09:32.660
I guess that's another Star Wars reference,
like when Luke left Yoda early to save his

00:09:32.660 --> 00:09:33.990
friends from Vader.

00:09:33.990 --> 00:09:38.600
I think we can all guess Mike and Bryan are
huge Star Wars fans, especially since the

00:09:38.600 --> 00:09:42.630
ended up casting Mark Hamill as the Emperor
Palpatine of their series

00:09:42.630 --> 00:09:44.839
Number 2 - Toph Beifong

00:09:44.839 --> 00:09:50.230
So many Toph questions still, her whereabouts
right now are still one of the biggest.

00:09:50.230 --> 00:09:53.250
But I'm so pumped to see her and Lin in the
flashbacks this year.

00:09:53.250 --> 00:10:00.250
I think my favorite Toph moment was when she
schooled Aang in sandbending a perfect replica

00:10:00.250 --> 00:10:02.810
of Ba Sing Se with one stomp of her foot.

00:10:02.810 --> 00:10:06.760
Has anyone ever wondered how often she had
to clean her feet when she started living

00:10:06.760 --> 00:10:07.760
in Republic City?

00:10:07.760 --> 00:10:13.200
I bet she had pretty gross feet walking around
without shoes all the time.

00:10:13.200 --> 00:10:17.520
It was pretty awesome when we got to see Lin
take her shoe off in book 1 and use the stomp

00:10:17.520 --> 00:10:18.520
echolocation Toph style.

00:10:18.520 --> 00:10:21.829
and my Number 1 favorite Last Airbender character
- Lord Zuko

00:10:21.829 --> 00:10:24.800
I say Lord just because he's not Firelord
anymore.

00:10:24.800 --> 00:10:28.760
He passed it on to his daughter, who we still
haven't met, even though we've met his grandson.

00:10:28.760 --> 00:10:32.810
Just like Toph, there are so many unanswered
Zuko questions right now.

00:10:32.810 --> 00:10:36.820
I think my favorite Zuko moment was actually
when he first decided to help Aang and was

00:10:36.820 --> 00:10:38.070
all like, "Hello, Zuko here!"

00:10:38.070 --> 00:10:39.550
and there were all these scary music cues.

00:10:39.550 --> 00:10:40.670
Dun Dun Dun.

00:10:40.670 --> 00:10:46.880
But let me know who you're favorite Last Airbender
character is and which one you want to see

00:10:46.880 --> 00:10:47.880
on Korra next.

00:10:47.880 --> 00:10:52.800
I know Toph is pretty high on everybody's
list.

00:10:52.800 --> 00:10:56.880
As a bonus, I'd say Cabbage Man is one of
my favorites.

00:10:56.880 --> 00:11:01.470
He's one of the best running gags on both
series.

00:11:01.470 --> 00:11:05.430
Back in book 1 I saw a bunch of theories that
Cabbage Corp was secretly going to be the

00:11:05.430 --> 00:11:07.280
ultimate villains of the new series.

00:11:07.280 --> 00:11:09.240
Which is funny to think about.

00:11:09.240 --> 00:11:14.340
We just saw him in Book 3 episode 1, he was
the one Korra almost hit with Asami's Car.

00:11:14.340 --> 00:11:18.130
So remember, two new episodes of Korra next
friday.

00:11:18.130 --> 00:11:19.230
Episodes 4 and 5.

00:11:19.230 --> 00:11:21.420
Because of the weird way they're doing episodes.

00:11:21.420 --> 00:11:24.820
I might combine my reviews of Episodes and
just do a Q&amp;A on saturdays instead of doing

00:11:24.820 --> 00:11:26.440
a review for each episode separately.

00:11:26.440 --> 00:11:28.370
Be sure to subscribe to get everything.

00:11:28.370 --> 00:11:33.570
Even if I do a review of two episodes in the
same video I'll still give away one gift card

00:11:33.570 --> 00:11:35.570
for each episode.

00:11:35.570 --> 00:11:39.760
Right now click here for my episode 1 and
2 video and click here for my episode 3 video.

00:11:39.760 --> 00:11:40.760
Thanks for watching, see you guys tomorrow.

00:11:40.760 --> 00:11:40.762
High Fives!

